      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors for Utah Homes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Climate Performance: Metal handles heavy mountain snow loads and sheds ice better\u2014crucial for bench and foothill areas like Draper, Alpine, or Summit County. High-altitude UV rays also degrade asphalt faster in Utah than national averages suggest ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Return on Investment: If you plan to stay in your home for 20+ years, a metal roof may pay for itself because you will avoid a second replacement cycle. If you plan to move within 10 years, asphalt provides better immediate financial return."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hidden Costs: Quotes may exclude extras like old layer removal, damaged decking repair, custom flashing around chimneys, or local Utah permit fees."
          }
        ]
